05:21.210 --> 05:25.953
and then git commit, delete most things.

05:26.940 --> 05:27.773
All righty.

05:27.773 --> 05:29.880
Now, if I wanna push the code that I just changed,

05:29.880 --> 05:33.210
I wanna push my last commit from this branch.

05:33.210 --> 05:35.520
Remember, I'm on the empty branch.

05:35.520 --> 05:38.010
I need to push the empty branch.

05:38.010 --> 05:40.230
So let me illustrate that here,

05:40.230 --> 05:41.970
I've got some diagrams.

05:41.970 --> 05:43.380
What we just did

05:43.380 --> 05:46.110
was we pushed up our master branch to GitHub.

05:46.110 --> 05:47.460
So there was nothing on GitHub.

05:47.460 --> 05:49.890
I pushed up master, whoops, I went too far.

05:49.890 --> 05:53.343
Git push origin master, assuming our remote is named origin.

05:54.210 --> 05:56.130
Now, in this diagram

05:56.130 --> 05:58.410
I have a second branch called new feature.

05:58.410 --> 05:59.760
I'm gonna push that up.

05:59.760 --> 06:02.283
Git push origin new feature.

06:03.150 --> 06:05.610
In our case, our branch is called empty.

06:05.610 --> 06:09.090
So git push origin empty.

06:09.090 --> 06:11.220
I don't have to be on this branch, by the way.

06:11.220 --> 06:14.130
I happen to be on it, which is very common that,

06:14.130 --> 06:15.900
you know, you're taking a look at what's on a branch

06:15.900 --> 06:16.920
and then you push it up

06:16.920 --> 06:18.630
but you don't have to be on it.

06:18.630 --> 06:20.583
So git push origin empty.

06:22.500 --> 06:25.260
And, remember, if it asks you for your password,

06:25.260 --> 06:26.670
not a big deal,

06:26.670 --> 06:29.430
put your email and password or your username and password.

06:29.430 --> 06:32.400
But go back and check out the SSH video

06:32.400 --> 06:35.220
