07:35.490 --> 07:37.140
Okay, pop quiz.

07:37.140 --> 07:38.070
What's on my GitHub?

07:38.070 --> 07:39.420
What's the most recent commit

07:39.420 --> 07:41.850
that I'll see on the GitHub repo?

07:41.850 --> 07:43.560
Nothing has changed on GitHub.

07:43.560 --> 07:45.420
It's still exactly the same.

07:45.420 --> 07:47.610
If we're looking at the master branch, nothing's changed.

07:47.610 --> 07:48.660
If we're looking at the empty branch,

07:48.660 --> 07:51.528
nothing has changed since we last pushed.

07:51.528 --> 07:54.390
GitHub doesn't just stay in sync automatically

07:54.390 --> 07:56.160
with my local repo.

07:56.160 --> 07:57.450
I have to push.

07:57.450 --> 08:00.090
So why don't I push up that commit?

08:00.090 --> 08:02.010
